## AC Workflow

An acceptance-criteria document defines one bounded change, its scope, and its tests. The short label AC refers both to that document and to the change it tracks.

Use `Draft → Audit → Refine → Implement → Ratify → Package` for an active AC. Draft writes the document. Audit challenges it without edits. Refine resolves findings in the document. Implement makes and verifies the settled change. Ratify performs final acceptance review. Package prepares the accepted change for release. Lowercase phase names and `package`, `pack`, or `prep` carry the same workflow meanings. Ordinary coding phrases such as `build`, `prepare the build`, and `package the binary` do not advance the workflow.
